WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.292 --> 00:00:02.750
-I lied right to
Bill Polian's face.

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:04.000
He said, "Have you
ever held before?"

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:04.958
And I said, "Absolutely."

00:00:04.958 --> 00:00:06.542
-What happened to the rest
of your hoodie?

00:00:06.542 --> 00:00:08.000
-It's arm farm, dude.
There's no sleeves allowed.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.417
-Somebody is trying to
chainsaw down our mailbox.

00:00:12.417 --> 00:00:14.667
♪♪

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:16.167
-That's it.

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:17.667
We're a quarter of the way
through the season.

00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:19.250
We know who's winning
the Super Bowl, Simms.

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:21.792
-Yep, we got it all figured out.
-Rams-Chiefs, 100 percent.

00:00:21.792 --> 00:00:25.417
Look, every year, one team
starts off really great

00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:27.625
another team doesn't,
and it's kind of become

00:00:27.625 --> 00:00:29.792
the first four weeks are like
the extended preseason.

00:00:29.792 --> 00:00:31.792
-Yes.
-And you've been telling me

00:00:31.792 --> 00:00:34.042
for the last few days,
it's for players, too.

00:00:34.042 --> 00:00:35.375
-Yeah, without a doubt.

00:00:35.375 --> 00:00:37.167
I mean, it's the new age
of the NFL.

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:39.417
We know with all the new rules
that players and the NFL has

00:00:39.417 --> 00:00:41.167
the coaching, the collective
bargaining agreement

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:43.625
the amount of hours and practices you can do—
-Right

00:00:43.625 --> 00:00:47.167
—in training camp, in OTAs,
that's hampered game plans.

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:49.042
But I think the other thing
that we are seeing

00:00:49.042 --> 00:00:51.792
especially this year,
we didn't see a lot of the stars

00:00:51.792 --> 00:00:53.500
a whole lot
through the preseason.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.000
We saw that this preseason.
-Yeah.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.250
-Where guys like
Ezekiel Elliott didn't play.

00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:58.500
Oh, you know what?

00:00:58.500 --> 00:00:59.875
Week 3 and 4,
all of the sudden

00:00:59.875 --> 00:01:01.792
he starts to go off.

00:01:01.792 --> 00:01:03.417
Jadeveon Clowney—I know he
was dealing with some injuries,

00:01:03.417 --> 00:01:05.292
but nobody wants to risk it.
Don't play preseason.

00:01:05.292 --> 00:01:06.875
-Right.
-Now, all of the sudden

00:01:06.875 --> 00:01:08.625
he plays the Indianapolis Colts
last Sunday

00:01:08.625 --> 00:01:10.667
and we see the beast
of Clowney unleashed again.

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:12.167
-Two sacks, fumble recovery for a touchdown.
-Exactly right.

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:13.542
So, I think this is something

00:01:13.542 --> 00:01:15.042
that we have to look at
going forward.

00:01:15.042 --> 00:01:17.542
Alvin Kamara—I know
he's had some moments

00:01:17.542 --> 00:01:18.917
through the first three weeks

00:01:18.917 --> 00:01:21.000
but last week
against the Giants

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.667
he was a different guy,
exploding through the hole.

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:26.500
So I do think the early part of
the season, with the new rules

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.792
and coaches not wanting
their stars to get hurt—

00:01:28.792 --> 00:01:30.125
-Yeah.

00:01:30.125 --> 00:01:31.750
-The star players
are not really

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:34.458
getting into their prime form
until Week 3, 4, 5.

00:01:34.458 --> 00:01:36.375
Earl Thomas didn't play
that much.

00:01:36.375 --> 00:01:39.000
Unfortunately, he's not playing
again the rest of this season

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.125
and he showed
the Seattle sideline

00:01:41.125 --> 00:01:45.000
how he really feels with this—
the state bird of New Jersey.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.417
-Yes.
-A middle finger

00:01:46.417 --> 00:01:48.333
probably right in the 
direction of Pete Carroll.

00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:50.625
And we wondered
what other NFL players

00:01:50.625 --> 00:01:52.750
would love
to give people the bird.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.500
I'm gonna let you go first.
-OK.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.375
-Young guy,
been takin' a lot of grief.

00:01:59.375 --> 00:02:01.000
-Right. Oh, Mitchell Trubisky!

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.250
Yeah, he's givin'
the middle finger.

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:03.500
You know who he's giving it to?

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:04.833
-Who?
-The Bears fans.

00:02:04.833 --> 00:02:06.250
First of all,
"Oh, we don't know.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:07.750
Is Mitchell Trubisky good?
Is he elite?"

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:10.000
He's giving it to his own coach,
Matt Nagy, goin',

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.625
"Oh, I don't have the full scope
of the offense?

00:02:12.625 --> 00:02:15.375
Hey, take this!
Six touchdowns, everybody!

00:02:15.375 --> 00:02:17.125
Back the eff off!"

00:02:17.125 --> 00:02:20.458
-I'm goin' quarterback as well,
and it's, yeah, Fitzpatrick

00:02:20.458 --> 00:02:24.333
and he's flipping this bird
squarely at Dirk Koetter's dome.

00:02:24.333 --> 00:02:25.875
Dirk Koetter comes out to
the game and says

00:02:25.875 --> 00:02:27.500
"I should be fired."
You know what?

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.125
Fitzpatrick agrees.

00:02:29.125 --> 00:02:32.000
Your defense allows 35 points
in the first half.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.625
Let's bench the quarterback.
That's the issue.

00:02:34.625 --> 00:02:36.500
All right, where you going?
-Ohhh.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:37.958
Good old Jersey Joe Flacco.

00:02:37.958 --> 00:02:39.500
He knows how to give
the middle finger.

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:40.875
He's saying, "Up yours

00:02:40.875 --> 00:02:42.500
Baltimore,
and all football fans.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:44.375
You can keep Lamar Jackson
on the bench.

00:02:44.375 --> 00:02:46.875
He can come in and run a few
gadget plays every now and then.

00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:49.375
We're 3-1, and we might be
in the Super Bowl."

00:02:49.375 --> 00:02:51.750
I like it. He's givin' it
to 'em right now.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:53.333
-I feel like
this is to similar people.

00:02:53.333 --> 00:02:55.458
-Yeah.
-This is to everyone that likes

00:02:55.458 --> 00:02:58.500
to talk about the impending doom
of Andy Dalton.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:01.125
-"He can't win the playoffs."
-"He can never get by!"

00:03:01.125 --> 00:03:02.750
All right.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:04.583
Well, under Bill Lazor,
he's been a revelation.

00:03:04.583 --> 00:03:07.500
He's connecting with A.J. Green.
He's connecting with Tyler Boyd.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.000
He doesn't even have Joe Mixon
-Right.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.250
-And he's doin' this
with Giovani Bernard.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.458
He's looked great.
Andy Dalton to the haters.

00:03:14.458 --> 00:03:17.625
And a finger,
and then another finger.
-[Laughing]

00:03:17.625 --> 00:03:19.000
-OK, gimme another one.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.750
-How about Saquon

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:22.375
and Odell Beckham Jr.
-Triple bird.

00:03:22.375 --> 00:03:24.125
-Saquon's goin', "Eli,
can you stop throwin' me

00:03:24.125 --> 00:03:25.833
the ball one yard
behind the line of scrimmage,

00:03:25.833 --> 00:03:27.208
and then I have to
play dodgeball

00:03:27.208 --> 00:03:28.750
and make everybody
on the defense miss?

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:30.208
I'm getting killed out here."

00:03:30.208 --> 00:03:31.750
And Odell Beckham Jr.'s goin',

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:34.000
"Can you just stand there
in the pocket?

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.375
I'm open downfield.

00:03:35.375 --> 00:03:37.250
There's some one-on-one shots."

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.875
And I think even Pat Shurmur,
he's goin'

00:03:38.875 --> 00:03:40.750
"Can you please teach
the O-line to block better

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:42.125
so we can throw
the ball down the field?"

00:03:42.125 --> 00:03:43.833
-Man, they're flickin' off everybody.
-Three, triple bird.

00:03:43.833 --> 00:03:45.500
-I got one more for you.
-You got one more?

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:48.750
-Superbird! Blake Bortles.

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:50.375
This was a middle finger
Blake wink to you.

00:03:50.375 --> 00:03:52.625
-Yeah, this was a,
"F--k you, Chris Simms" week.

00:03:52.625 --> 00:03:55.500
He should just get S-I-M-M-S
on his middle finger.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.333
-I like that.
-And when he has a good week

00:03:57.333 --> 00:04:00.000
he can just put it right up
there and tell me to shut up.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.250
-You and Bortles,
not best football friends.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:04.125
-No, we're not.
-Us?

00:04:04.125 --> 00:04:06.625
Big-time best football friends,
and we took our act on the road

00:04:06.625 --> 00:04:09.333
to take on the 49els.
The Ninels.

00:04:09.333 --> 00:04:10.875
-The Ninels?
-Can you finish that, my friend?

00:04:10.875 --> 00:04:13.542
-49ers.
-Thank you.

00:04:13.542 --> 00:04:15.917
-You may shower together, but
we feel like we got you beat.

00:04:15.917 --> 00:04:17.792
-Yeah, I think so, too.
-You guys don't?

00:04:17.792 --> 00:04:19.917
-No, no.
-That kinda takes it to the next level.
-That's really weird.

00:04:19.917 --> 00:04:25.000
♪♪

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.292
-How'd you guys meet?

00:04:26.292 --> 00:04:28.250
-We worked out
every single day together

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:30.417
and then somehow got drafted to
the same team in the same round

00:04:30.417 --> 00:04:32.417
like, 15 picks apart
from each other.

00:04:32.417 --> 00:04:34.250
-Wow.
-As soon as I got drafted

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:37.542
instantly, George
on the FaceTime, just, "Ahhh!"

00:04:37.542 --> 00:04:38.792
yellin' into the camera.

00:04:38.792 --> 00:04:40.292
So it was a good time.

00:04:40.292 --> 00:04:44.042
-That's a cute
little love story.

00:04:44.042 --> 00:04:45.792
-This is about to be
a piece of cake.

00:04:45.792 --> 00:04:48.167
-Can someone make sure
they're not cheating?

00:04:48.167 --> 00:04:50.625
Oh.
-Oh, nice little warm-up

00:04:50.625 --> 00:04:52.292
for you guys.
That's so cute too.

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:54.417
-Do I turn?
-Yeah, let's see.

00:04:54.417 --> 00:04:55.667
-Bam!

00:04:55.667 --> 00:04:57.542
I hope they get harder
than this.

00:05:00.292 --> 00:05:02.125
-Got it.

00:05:02.125 --> 00:05:04.792
-Yay!
-Oh, gosh.

00:05:04.792 --> 00:05:07.167
This is layups for these two.

00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:09.167
-Yeah.
-Did you really?

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:11.500
-Yeah, baby.
-What did you run?

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:12.875
-4.52.

00:05:12.875 --> 00:05:14.917
-Wow! And Trent,
what did you have?

00:05:14.917 --> 00:05:17.167
-I ran a 4-ever.
-[Laughing]

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:20.542
Something like that.
-Oh, no.

00:05:20.542 --> 00:05:23.417
-Don't cheat.
-I'm so bad at this.

00:05:23.417 --> 00:05:25.292
Damn it.
-It's embarrassing.

00:05:25.292 --> 00:05:26.542
-It is embarrassing.
-I know yours.

00:05:26.542 --> 00:05:27.875
-I know you know mine.

00:05:27.875 --> 00:05:29.542
That's why I'm even
more embarrassed.

00:05:29.542 --> 00:05:32.667
-These are the moments when
you question your friendship.

00:05:32.667 --> 00:05:38.250
-It seems like it's around here.
-What did he guess?

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:39.917
-About as far away
as you possibly can get.

00:05:39.917 --> 00:05:41.292
-You just—
like, you would know

00:05:41.292 --> 00:05:42.667
if my birthday
was New Year's Eve.

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:44.625
-You seem like a December guy.
I just—

00:05:44.625 --> 00:05:46.750
-I seem—
-You seem like a December guy.

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:49.167
-You seem like a former friend.
-Damn.

00:05:49.167 --> 00:05:50.792
-What happened to the rest
of your hoodie?

00:05:50.792 --> 00:05:53.792
-It's arm farm, dude.
There's no sleeves allowed.
-Arm farm?

00:05:55.042 --> 00:05:56.167
-Oh, I tweeted that.

00:05:56.167 --> 00:05:58.875
♪♪

00:05:58.875 --> 00:06:01.208
-Stop!

00:06:01.208 --> 00:06:02.625
-Y'all are givin' me good hints
right now

00:06:02.625 --> 00:06:04.458
so I'm gonna go
for something like this.

00:06:04.458 --> 00:06:07.625
-Oh!
-You were close.

00:06:07.625 --> 00:06:09.583
-♪ I want Candy ♪

00:06:09.583 --> 00:06:11.000
♪ Bum, ba-dum, ba-dum, bum, bum ♪

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.958
-That was a jam back in the day.
-It was a jam.

00:06:12.958 --> 00:06:16.458
See, I remember things
about you, unlike my birthday.

00:06:16.458 --> 00:06:17.708
-Dude, I'm embarrassed about
the birthday thing.

00:06:17.708 --> 00:06:20.125
-I expect a present.

00:06:20.125 --> 00:06:22.833
Rice, beans, peppers,
sometimes hot sauce

00:06:22.833 --> 00:06:24.458
multiple scoops of rice and beans.

00:06:24.458 --> 00:06:27.375
-That's crazy.

00:06:27.375 --> 00:06:29.250
-Yeah.
-Orange chicken.
-Let's go, baby!

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:30.958
-Orange chicken!
-But you go a double orange chicken?

00:06:30.958 --> 00:06:32.708
-I was honestly about
to put double orange chicken.

00:06:32.708 --> 00:06:34.583
-Sweet and fire, honey walnut
shrimp, honey sesame.

00:06:34.583 --> 00:06:36.000
I'll switch it up.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.208
-How much money do you spend
at Panda Express?

00:06:38.208 --> 00:06:39.875
-I like Chinese food a lot.
-Yeah.

00:06:39.875 --> 00:06:41.375
-I feel like our connection's

00:06:41.375 --> 00:06:42.625
definitely better than theirs
at this point.

00:06:42.625 --> 00:06:43.958
-Oh, you do?
-More fluid.

00:06:43.958 --> 00:06:45.375
Theirs is forced.

00:06:45.375 --> 00:06:47.875
-Oh, yeah, I play quarterback.

00:06:47.875 --> 00:06:49.208
Omaha, blue, go!

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:50.875
-Peyton Manning.
-Thank you.

00:06:50.875 --> 00:06:52.125
-Greatest quarterback
of all time.

00:06:52.125 --> 00:06:55.250
-Aaron Rodgers.
-Oh, my turn.

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:57.625
We won the Hall of Fame.
He's close to me. He's a relative.

00:06:57.625 --> 00:06:59.000
-Phil Simms.
-Right.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.833
-Overdrafted by
the Dallas Cowboys.

00:07:00.833 --> 00:07:02.875
White linebacker.

00:07:02.875 --> 00:07:04.708
-Three seconds!
-Oh, Leighton Vander Esch.

00:07:04.708 --> 00:07:06.208
-Go.
-Oh, my old coach! "Spider 2 Y Banana!"

00:07:06.208 --> 00:07:08.625
-Jon Gruden! Jon Gruden!
-Time's up.

00:07:08.625 --> 00:07:10.625
-[Laughing]
-Jon Gruden! Did that get in?

00:07:10.625 --> 00:07:13.125
-That was awesome.

00:07:13.125 --> 00:07:16.375
-Um, quarterback for the 49ers.

00:07:16.375 --> 00:07:18.125
-Jimmy Garoppolo.

00:07:18.125 --> 00:07:20.083
Our best friend on the team.
Lived with us last year.

00:07:20.083 --> 00:07:22.500
-JP Flynn.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:24.250
-Celebration.
-Stone Cold Steve Austin.

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:25.875
-Damn!
-These are a lot easier
than your guys'.

00:07:25.875 --> 00:07:28.333
-Just came out with an album.
Everybody listens to him.

00:07:28.333 --> 00:07:31.125
-Drake?
-Yes.

00:07:31.125 --> 00:07:33.708
-Um, he put my stapler in Jello.
No, no, no.

00:07:33.708 --> 00:07:35.083
-Dwight Schrute.
-Yeah.

00:07:35.083 --> 00:07:36.875
-I can't believe
we're tied right now.

00:07:36.875 --> 00:07:38.750
♪♪

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:40.792
-[Whispering] We need to create a
good structural base.

00:07:40.792 --> 00:07:42.792
-Agreed.
-OK, good

00:07:44.583 --> 00:07:47.625
-What?
-How do we do this?
-Wow.

00:07:47.625 --> 00:07:50.875
-We can do this.
-Hands up.

00:07:50.875 --> 00:07:52.250
Go.
-OK.

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:54.375
-Big base here.
Do what you said.

00:07:54.375 --> 00:07:58.083
-OK, big base here.
-Stop cheating, Trent.

00:07:58.083 --> 00:07:59.500
♪♪

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:00.833
-You're going to
the second level.
-No, I'm not.

00:08:00.833 --> 00:08:02.375
That's not the base.
-Break these in half.

00:08:02.375 --> 00:08:03.958
-Let's get all the ones
in the base and then go from there.

00:08:03.958 --> 00:08:05.625
-Trust me, bro.
-OK, fine.

00:08:05.625 --> 00:08:07.375
I don't know what you're doing.
-You seem flustered.

00:08:07.375 --> 00:08:08.833
-You've taken it upon yourself
to do what you want to do.

00:08:08.833 --> 00:08:10.583
-Trust me.
-Yeah, you think?

00:08:10.583 --> 00:08:12.000
-You're a base. "You're a towel."
-OK.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:13.833
What, do you wanna connect it
over there?

00:08:13.833 --> 00:08:16.458
-Oh, sh—This is not...

00:08:16.458 --> 00:08:18.125
Holy crap.
-Lefkoe.

00:08:18.125 --> 00:08:19.750
-Gimme another one,
gimme another one.

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:21.750
-Are we gonna go any higher?
-This one?
-Yes, it's fine.

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:24.625
-Gimme this thing.

00:08:24.625 --> 00:08:27.000
♪♪

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:28.625
-Hands up, Lefkoe.
-What's up, guys?

00:08:28.625 --> 00:08:30.750
-Are you f--king kidding me?
-Why didn't we just—that's
what I wanted to do!

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:32.750
-The champs are here, baby!

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:34.125
Let's go!
-Wooo!

00:08:34.125 --> 00:08:37.625
-Still structurally—

00:08:37.625 --> 00:08:39.375
-Wow, look at that structure.
-Stand strong, baby.

00:08:39.375 --> 00:08:40.875
-Let's go!
-I'm really sorry.

00:08:40.875 --> 00:08:42.625
-It's all right.
-Wooo!

00:08:42.625 --> 00:08:46.250
-I should've known
your birthday too.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:48.958
♪♪

00:08:48.958 --> 00:08:51.375
-So, we took our first L—
Kittle and Trent Taylor.

00:08:51.375 --> 00:08:53.208
-Jeez.
-Forgot my birthday.

00:08:53.208 --> 00:08:54.875
-Well, because you decided to go, like,
diva wide receiver at the end

00:08:54.875 --> 00:08:57.458
and build your own spaghetti—
you didn't listen.

00:08:57.458 --> 00:08:58.833
No teamwork.

00:08:58.833 --> 00:09:00.083
-He has no idea
what we're talking about.

00:09:00.083 --> 00:09:01.708
-Well, it's all right.

00:09:01.708 --> 00:09:03.500
-I want him to be our third
best football friend, Pat McAfee.

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:05.625
